# Paths stow must not link out of this package.
#
# Providing this file REPLACES stow's built-in default ignore list, so the
# defaults are repeated below -- drop them and stow will start linking .git,
# editor backups and so on into $HOME.
#
# Patterns containing a slash are matched against the path relative to this
# package directory, anchored at both ends; patterns without one are matched
# against basenames anywhere in the tree.

# pkg/ is a build tree, not dotfiles. Without this stow creates ~/pkg as a
# symlink into the repo, which is meaningless -- `make -C ~/dotfiles/linux/pkg`
# is how it is used. This went unnoticed for a long time only because stow
# aborted on other conflicts before it ever got here.
^/pkg$

# stow's defaults, verbatim.
RCS
.+,v
CVS
\.\#.+
\.cvsignore
\.svn
_darcs
\.hg
\.git
\.gitignore
\.gitmodules
.+~
\#.*\#
^/README.*
^/LICENSE.*
^/COPYING
